**Day 37: MongoDB Schema Design**  

**Topic:**  
Understanding schema design in MongoDB, focusing on embedding vs. referencing documents and applying schema design patterns for beginners.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Compare embedding vs. referencing documents for optimal data relationships.  
• Design schemas for blog posts (embedded comments) and orders (referenced).  
• Apply schema patterns to real-world scenarios.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Design a schema for blog posts with embedded comments.  
• Create a schema for orders with referenced customer details.  
• Visualize schema relationships using Draw.io.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **Embedding:** Stores related data within a single document (e.g., comments inside a blog post).  
• **Referencing:** Uses document IDs to link related data (e.g., orders referencing customer IDs).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `db.createCollection("blog_posts")`  
• `db.orders.insertOne({ customerId: ObjectId("..."), items: [...] })`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Blog platforms (embedded comments for faster reads).  
• E-commerce systems (referenced orders for scalability).  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• MongoDB  
• MongoDB Compass  
• Draw.io  

**Summary:**  
Learned to design efficient MongoDB schemas by choosing between embedding and referencing based on use cases. Practiced with blog posts (embedded) and orders (referenced), and visualized schemas using Draw.io.  

